@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Boards, Queries, and Charts";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Azure DevOps provides powerful visualization tools such as **Boards, Queries, and Charts** to help teams track and analyze work progress effectively.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Azure Boards: Visualizing Work Items</h2>
        <p>Azure Boards provide a **Kanban-style** interface to manage work items efficiently. It allows teams to visualize their workflow, track progress, and optimize work distribution.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Supports **drag-and-drop functionality** to update work item statuses.</li>
            <li>Configurable **columns** to represent different workflow stages (To-Do, In Progress, Done).</li>
            <li>Facilitates **work-in-progress limits** to prevent task overload.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/boards-kanban.png" alt="Azure Boards" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Kanban Board in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Managing Work Using Azure Boards</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Track progress using **swimlanes** for different work categories.</li>
                <li>Apply **custom tags and filters** for better visualization.</li>
                <li>Enable **real-time collaboration** and updates.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Queries: Customizing Work Item Tracking</h2>
        <p>Azure DevOps Queries help teams filter and retrieve specific work items based on criteria such as status, priority, and assigned users.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Supports **basic and advanced query builders**.</li>
            <li>Enables **saved queries** for quick access.</li>
            <li>Facilitates **automated reporting and tracking**.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Using Queries Effectively</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Filter work items based on **team priorities**.</li>
                <li>Use **AND/OR conditions** to refine search results.</li>
                <li>Export queries for external reporting.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/query-builder.png" alt="Query Builder in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Query Builder for Filtering Work Items</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Charts: Data-Driven Insights</h2>
        <p>Azure DevOps Charts provide **visual reports** on work progress, helping teams make informed decisions based on project data.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Supports **Pie Charts, Bar Charts, and Trend Lines**.</li>
            <li>Displays work distribution across teams.</li>
            <li>Enhances decision-making with real-time insights.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/charts-reporting.png" alt="Charts and Reporting in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Charts for Visualizing Work Progress</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Best Practices for Using Charts</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Use **Burndown Charts** to monitor sprint progress.</li>
                <li>Analyze **Cumulative Flow Diagrams** to identify bottlenecks.</li>
                <li>Share reports with stakeholders for **better transparency**.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps provides **Boards, Queries, and Charts** to help teams manage and visualize work efficiently. Leveraging these tools ensures **better tracking, prioritization, and reporting** for Agile projects.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **What is CI/CD? and Build Pipelines in Azure DevOps**.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-start mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("SprintPlanningBacklogManagement", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Sprint Planning & Backlog Management</a>
    </div>
</div>
